The hold ended with
  aie.utils.hostruntime.hostruntime.HostRuntimeError: Kernel returned ert_cmd_state.ERT_CMD_STATE_TIMEOUT
about 7 s into its 5000 iterations, and the process then sat in XRT's wait until 23:49:11.
The "busy stretch" statistics are therefore not a utilization measurement; they are the
ramp (~7 s of 82-94 %, the same band as run 1), the hang (0 %), and single 100 % samples
scattered through the wait. What they do establish is the period: 0.100 / 0.250 / 0.500 s
with min = max at the 10 ms print, at all three rates, for ~2 minutes.

Why it hung -- attributed, not assumed. The monitor's own first lines show a hardware
context ALREADY on the device before this hold started, with 1.9 GB allocated:
